# SEO cluster landing pages

Supporting long-tail pages that embed an existing tool. They are not new products.

Reference: `/remove-background-from-image` wrapping Make Background Transparent.

## Do not register as a tool

Never add the page to `data/tools.ts`, `data/related-tools.ts`, homepage grids, category listings, or search catalogs. Register only in `data/seo-landings.ts` (sitemap already maps that array).

## Look like the parent tool

Reuse `ToolLayout` + the parent’s lazy editor. Keep the parent `slug` on the display tool so analytics, feedback, and “You may also be interested in:” resolve to the parent’s 3 related tools.

Override only: `name` (H1), `shortName`, `description` (one sentence), `href`, `faq`.

Hero must match the parent:

- Eyebrow: `Free tool` (comes from `ToolLayout`)
- H1: unique, keyword-natural, tool-name style
- Lede: one sentence, same shape as the parent description

Landing body must use the parent’s section order (see `MakeBackgroundTransparentLanding`): FeatureGrid → How It Works (intro + 3 steps + in-page jump) → Popular Use Cases → Related Free Tools → FAQ. Unique copy only. CTA same pattern as the parent.

## Parent tool button

Every SEO landing must show a normal primary button to the parent tool, placed immediately above the “Found a bug…” line. The label is the parent’s full `name` (e.g. `Make Background Transparent`, `QR Code Generator`). `ToolLayout` renders this automatically when `displayTool.href` differs from the catalog tool — do not omit it, and do not explain that this is an SEO page.

## Copy rules

- Write useful product text. Do not say this is an SEO page, funnel, cluster, or “not a real tool”.
- Do not name other brands (Canva, Figma, Photoshop, etc.).
- Title includes the keyword plus “online” and “free” when natural.
- FAQ: same topics/count as the parent, rewritten for the keyword.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — parent slug, unique name/lede/faq, same shell
const displayTool = { ...parentTool, name: page.h1, shortName: page.shortName, description: page.description, href: page.href, faq: page.faq };
<ToolAnalyticsProvider toolId={parentTool.slug}>
  <ToolLayout tool={displayTool} workspaceId={`${page.slug}-tool`} content={<SeoLanding />} ctaTitle={...} ctaDescription={...}>
    <ParentToolLazy />
  </ToolLayout>
</ToolAnalyticsProvider>

// ❌ BAD — custom shell, multi-paragraph intro, no related-tool cards, “this is not a separate tool”
```
